Subject: Asphalt 7: Heat starts and runs (tiles, managed component stand-ins, SettingsPane, DisplayProperties, StreamSocket, SwapChainBackgroundPanel, IInspectable proxy)

What Asphalt 7 (a Windows 8.1 XAML app with a SwapChainBackgroundPanel) needed:
- wpnapps: TileUpdateManager, TileUpdater and TileNotification; stand-ins for its managed components that Windows hosts
  with CLRHost.dll (NotificationsExtensions' tile content for a wide and a square image tile, and GA.GoogleAnalytics);
  an Accelerometer that is absent (GetDefault gives null)
- windows.ui: Windows.UI.ApplicationSettings.SettingsPane
- windows.ui.xaml: SwapChainBackgroundPanel (a SwapChainPanel with ISwapChainBackgroundPanelNative), Window.SizeChanged
  raised, and SizeChanged and VisibilityChanged raised a moment after Activate() as on Windows (the game sets itself
  up on other threads from its Activated handler and its VisibilityChanged handler uses what they make)
- windows.graphics: Windows.Graphics.Display.DisplayProperties
- windows.networking: StreamSocket (connecting fails as offline) and StreamSocketListener (binds, never connects)
- windows.storage.applicationdata: ApplicationDataContainer.CreateContainer
- twinapi.appcore: ApplicationView.Value and TryUnsnap
- actxprxy: IInspectable's proxy and stub, which the proxy/stub DLLs that apps declare delegate to

